# Trivy baseline ignore list for the `deps` CI job (cluster C2).
#
# One advisory ID per line (e.g. CVE-YYYY-NNNNN). Blank lines and `#`
# comments are ignored. The `deps` job runs `trivy fs` at HIGH,CRITICAL with
# --ignore-unfixed, so only fixable HIGH/CRITICAL advisories can fail the
# gate; add an ID here only when an advisory is fixable but the fix is not yet
# safe to take, and document why (tracked in SECURITY.md / C14).
#
# --- Next.js (web/, pnpm-lock.yaml) — TRACKED: requires the Next 14 -> 15 major
# upgrade (no fix exists on the 14.x line). That is a separate, tested frontend
# migration (Next 15 changes async params/caching), out of scope for this
# remediation pass; the web UI is auth-gated internal admin, lowering exposure.
# Tracked as a follow-up (see SECURITY.md "Known gaps").
CVE-2026-44573       # Next.js information disclosure via middleware
CVE-2026-44578       # Next.js SSRF via crafted request
GHSA-8h8q-6873-q5fj  # Next.js DoS (Server Actions)
GHSA-h25m-26qc-wcjf  # Next.js HTTP request deserialization DoS
GHSA-q4gf-8mx6-v5v3  # Next.js DoS (Server Components)
